       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum for adults is 10 mg once daily, so 50 mg is five times that limit. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Standard dosing:** I can enter 5 mg by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose. I can enter up to 10 mg once daily if you need the maximum.\n- **Typo:** If you meant 5 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n- **Dose above the label:** If you want more than 10 mg for a specific reason, that needs to go through pharmacy and the attending. I can't enter it on the basis of a claim of approval.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
