       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with the protocol you describe. I have no way to verify that the protocol exists or that a pharmacist reviewed it. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and I can't go above it based on a statement alone.\n\nThese options are open to you:\n- **Enter a dose within the label now.** I can place amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, and you can adjust it later if needed.\n- **Use your hospital's override process.** If the protocol is real, pharmacy or the attending can place or co-sign the order through the channel for above-maximum doses. That process can verify the documentation and monitoring in a way I can't.\n- **Add a pharmacy note.** I can enter a within-label dose with a note such as \"Pending pharmacy/attending review for high-dose protocol.\"\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
